        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                "word": "duodénum",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "adcbc96b-98e1-4c00-904a-f3275950d9c2",
                        "entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "duodénums"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                        "entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Partie qui relie l’estomac à l’intestin grêle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32530e71-e787-449d-84bf-329fad922031",
                                "sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                                "text": "Trois gresles, appelés duodenum, jejunum et ileon […] le premier a esté ainsi nommé, à cause qu’il est quasi comme un changement de ventricule en intestin, selon la longitude de douze doigts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "120b84cb-089d-4692-b863-049b64804366",
                                "sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                                "text": "En arrière du foie, on trouve le ligament hépato-gastrique, qui fixe l'estomac dans la scissure postérieure du foie; ce frein se prolonge à droite et en arrière, attache le duodénum à la face inférieure du rein droit, puis se dirige de droite à gauche, en se continuant avec le péritoine pariétal de la région sous-lombaire et le mésentère proprement dit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3b017ef-dc95-43a3-a367-4c33492a5c68",
                                "sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                                "text": "Après les repas le contenu gastrique acide s’évacue par intermittence dans le duodénum. Et le contact de ce bol alimentaire acide avec la muqueuse duodénale déclenche l’ouverture du sphincter d’Oddi et la contraction de la vésicule qui chasse la bile vers l’intestin."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "19d5d0ad-9293-40a8-af33-f182ef9872ed",
                        "source_entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                        "source_sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                        "target_lang_word": "Duodenum",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Duodenum",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "badcf5a8-82b5-3592-bc47-3d36d8ebf90c",
                                        "entry_id": "5ba0bf1a-eb1a-3502-bfaf-8d58d2dc997a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zwölffingerdarm; Teil des Dünndarms"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ccf33a3-3ede-4c87-a84b-a07c33b35dbd",
                                                "sense_id": "badcf5a8-82b5-3592-bc47-3d36d8ebf90c",
                                                "text": "„Das Duodenum ist der sich dem Magen anschliessende, am weitesten oral gelegene Teil des Dünndarmes.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64820e99-f5ff-4f1c-88a9-6bf1cbfe61ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                        "source_sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                        "target_lang_word": "Zwölffingerdarm",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Zwölffingerdarm",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3917d5e7-2750-3542-95f8-2150c75e026f",
                                        "entry_id": "cd5eb085-fb8a-328f-8ec9-c8920c445f0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "erster Abschnitt des Dünndarms"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aefd784c-3742-4d7c-bba7-bfe6dfaf6fd0",
                                                "sense_id": "3917d5e7-2750-3542-95f8-2150c75e026f",
                                                "text": "Der Arzt kann mit einem Endoskop die Speiseröhre, den Magen und den Zwölffingerdarm betrachten."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a179ae2e-f6ac-448e-a12f-f9dba977fdab",
                        "source_entry_id": "202ce92f-87de-37c1-be48-320604b6f3d8",
                        "source_sense_id": "f4e17224-d55c-30cf-9174-982ecb36ac19",
                        "target_lang_word": "duodenum",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "duodenum",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                        "entry_id": "49d28d25-b0b3-34b6-bc00-e7079c197936",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The first part of the small intestine, starting at the lower end of the stomach and extending to the jejunum."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e8b2775-8cd2-4176-92e8-c756f738fc42",
                                                "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                                "text": "From the Stomacke to the very Fundament, are produced the Guts or Inteſtina, which ſerue a little to alter and diſtribute the Chilus, and convey away the excrements. They are divided into ſmall and great, by reason of their ſite and ſubſtance, ſlender or thicker. The ſlender is Duodenum or whole gut, which is next to the ſtomacke, ſome twelue inches long (ſaith Fuſchius.)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee4e49d9-3901-4834-8793-be65377f63fa",
                                                "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                                "text": "The Inteſtina tenuia were burnt in many places, but not quite through any where, excepting two or three. […] The length of that which is commonly call'd the Duodenum, was about 4½ Foot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19394c5f-67eb-4d1a-9625-6dc0d749dbf6",
                                                "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                                "text": "The duodenum receives the chyme from the stomach, and has generally been believed to accomplish the second digestion, or the conversion of chyme into chyle. In the duodenum it meets with the bile, pancreatic and intestinal fluids, loses its acid properties, and becomes alkaline, probably by the agency of the soda of the bile; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a912be53-11b3-473b-a354-0d15dbae79f0",
                                                "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                                "text": "The duodena open into a common pouch just below the entrance of the gall-ducts. The intestine was single from the confluence of the duodena to the termination of the jejunum."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba8799cd-7286-4e89-ac9e-eee7dfeb78d0",
                                                "sense_id": "61a5b895-c763-335b-9269-bf791129ef27",
                                                "text": "Duodenums were dissected out, fixed and photographed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
